# Invariant 6 and POST /proposal: a member that uploads the same proposal twice - a retry of an
# upload whose answer it lost - is answered as the first time. Member proposals carry no nonce, so
# carol's second `leave` in the same epoch is byte-identical to the first: the instance answers it
# with the first upload's seq, writes and fans out nothing again, and alice's commit applies the one
# Remove. carol keeps her proposal (a refusal would have made her withdraw it), so she can process
# the commit that removes her.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group chat kind=text target=dfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdf community=none creator=alice
join bob chat via=welcome
join carol chat via=welcome
sync bob
sync carol
leave carol chat
leave carol chat
commit alice chat
sync bob
sync carol
send alice chat carol has left
expect_decrypts bob chat carol has left
